From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] boot-splash: NickelOS's boot animation when the image has
 one

frecon shows ChromiumOS's frames from chromiumos-assets while the system
starts. NickelOS's own (chromeos-bsp-nickel, /usr/share/nickel/boot-splash)
are taken instead when they're there, with the same frame interval and the
same 100% and 200% sets.

---
diff -ruN a/init/upstart/boot-splash.conf b/init/upstart/boot-splash.conf
--- a/init/upstart/boot-splash.conf
+++ b/init/upstart/boot-splash.conf
@@ -56,6 +56,13 @@
       ASSETS_100=${ASSETS}/animated_splash_screen/splash_100_percent
     fi
 
+    # NickelOS: its own boot animation, when the image has one
+    # (chromeos-bsp-nickel installs it beside ChromiumOS's).
+    if [ -e /usr/share/nickel/boot-splash/images_100_percent/boot_splash_frame01.png ]; then
+      ASSETS_200=/usr/share/nickel/boot-splash/images_200_percent
+      ASSETS_100=/usr/share/nickel/boot-splash/images_100_percent
+    fi
+
     if [ -f "${ASSETS}/splash_background" ]; then
       BACKGROUND=$(cat "${ASSETS}/splash_background")
     fi
